---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { localePath } from "../../i18n";
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../../lib/site";
const lang = "en" as const;
---

<Base lang={lang} title="Terms of Use — Recompendium" description="Terms of use for Recompendium: what the site is, third-party trademarks, data accuracy, and content takedowns.">
  <main class="wrap detail">
    <div class="crumb"><a href={localePath(lang, "")}>← Catalog</a></div>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="lead">Recompendium is an informational, community-run, open-source catalog of console games running natively on PC. By using this site, you accept these terms.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
      <p>Recompendium is a nonprofit project that <b>lists and links to</b> third-party projects: static recompilations, decompilations, ports built on a decompilation, fan-made remakes, and tools. We don’t develop or distribute those projects: we only link to their public repositories.</p>

      <h2>2. No ROMs or copyrighted material</h2>
      <p>Recompendium <b>does not host, distribute, or link to</b> ROMs, BIOS files, or copyrighted assets. Each project is <b>code only</b>: you have to supply your own legal copy of the game. This site does not promote or facilitate piracy.</p>

      <h2>3. Trademarks and third-party content</h2>
      <p>Game, console, and company names are trademarks of their respective owners and are used only to identify them (nominative use). Recompendium is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them. Each linked project belongs to its authors and is governed by its own license.</p>

      <h2>4. Data accuracy</h2>
      <p>The catalog is maintained by the community and automatically supplemented with data from public APIs (GitHub and decomp.dev). The information (status, versions, stars, dates) may contain errors or be out of date, and it is provided <b>“as is,”</b> without any warranty of accuracy. Use your own judgment.</p>

      <h2>5. External links</h2>
      <p>We don’t control the linked sites or repositories, and we are not responsible for their content, availability, or practices.</p>

      <h2>6. Site intellectual property</h2>
      <p>The Recompendium code is released under the <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT license</a>. The catalog data are public facts about third-party projects.</p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>The site is provided “as is,” without warranties of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the site’s maintainers shall not be liable for any damages arising from the use of the site or of the linked projects.</p>

      <h2>8. Content takedown</h2>
      <p>If you are a rights holder and believe a link infringes your rights, <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">open an issue</a> in the repository and we’ll review it as soon as possible.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. The effective date indicates the latest revision.</p>

      <p class="upd">Effective as of October 12, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
